### Darb Portal — sample webhook requests
### Usable with the VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP Client.
### The email payloads here carry short inline base64; the full generated payloads with
### real fixture bytes live in fixtures/payloads/ and are fired by scripts/send-sample-webhooks.sh.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 1. WhatsApp — exact match. Every signal agrees → AUTO_MATCHED to transaction 1.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entry": [{
    "changes": [{
      "value": {
        "messages": [{
          "id": "wamid.HBgMOTY2NTUxMjM0NTY3AA==",
          "from": "966551234567",
          "timestamp": "1749899520",
          "type": "image",
          "image": { "id": "media_4471", "mime_type": "image/jpeg", "sha256": "a3f1c9" }
        }]
      }
    }]
  }]
}

### 2. The same message again — idempotency. Expect disposition DUPLICATE, no new document.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entry": [{
    "changes": [{
      "value": {
        "messages": [{
          "id": "wamid.HBgMOTY2NTUxMjM0NTY3AA==",
          "from": "966551234567",
          "timestamp": "1749899520",
          "type": "image",
          "image": { "id": "media_4471", "mime_type": "image/jpeg", "sha256": "a3f1c9" }
        }]
      }
    }]
  }]
}

### 3. WhatsApp — ambiguous. Two Tamimi transactions, same amount, same day → NEEDS_REVIEW.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entry": [{
    "changes": [{
      "value": {
        "messages": [{
          "id": "wamid.HBgMOTY2NTUxMjM0NTY4AA==",
          "from": "966551234567",
          "timestamp": "1750162200",
          "type": "image",
          "image": { "id": "media_4472", "mime_type": "image/jpeg", "sha256": "b7d2e1" }
        }]
      }
    }]
  }]
}

### 4. WhatsApp — scoping. A Nujood driver sends Rawabi's receipt; it must not match.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entry": [{
    "changes": [{
      "value": {
        "messages": [{
          "id": "wamid.HBgMOTY2NTYxMTEyMjMzAA==",
          "from": "966561112233",
          "timestamp": "1749899520",
          "type": "image",
          "image": { "id": "media_4471", "mime_type": "image/jpeg", "sha256": "a3f1c9" }
        }]
      }
    }]
  }]
}

### 5. WhatsApp — malformed. type says image but no image object → 400 with field-level issues.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entry": [{
    "changes": [{
      "value": {
        "messages": [{
          "id": "wamid.BROKEN",
          "from": "966551234567",
          "timestamp": "1749899520",
          "type": "image"
        }]
      }
    }]
  }]
}

### 6. Email — malformed. Bad address, no attachments → 400.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messageId": "",
  "from": "not-an-email",
  "to": "receipts@darb.example.com",
  "receivedAt": "nope",
  "attachments": []
}

### 7. Transactions — the re-match trigger.
### Fire request 4's orphan receipt first (it lands UNMATCHED), then this. The response
### reports which documents the new transaction rescued.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactions": [
    {
      "clientId": 1,
      "cardLast4": "4412",
      "driverPhone": "966551234567",
      "merchantName": "KUDU REST 118 RUH",
      "amount": 3300,
      "currency": "SAR",
      "transactionAt": "2025-06-19T13:12:00Z"
    }
  ]
}

### 8. Transactions — malformed. Returns 400 with one issue per bad field.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactions": [
    { "clientId": 1, "cardLast4": "44", "merchantName": "", "amount": -5, "transactionAt": "nope" }
  ]
}

### 9. Health checks
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/email

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp?hub.mode=subscribe&hub.challenge=12345
